    {
      "id": "PEO-009",
      "order": 90,
      "type": "design",
      "title": "Weighted-draw movement for the Dead with aggregates and company pull",
      "status": "Pending",
      "severity": "S2",
      "effort": "L",
      "owner": "architect",
      "created": "2026-09-28",
      "notes": [
        {
          "at": "2026-09-28",
          "by": "architect",
          "text": "D-007 (see decisions.md) fixes the shape of the draw: weight a candidate cell by pow(scent, k) with a tunable exponent k slightly above 1, never exp(k*scent) — at the 0-500 scale from PEO-026 exp saturates immediately. A power law keys off the ratio between neighbouring cells, so one k stays decisive next to the player and becomes a gentle drift far away, which is the horde-drift behaviour the user asked for. Fold this into the brief when PEO-009 is planned."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-09-29",
          "by": "architect",
          "text": "PEO-007 constraint: World::commit re-decides only the Dead within 2 cells of the player, so a Dead's decision must not depend on how many others decided before it. The weighted draw must take its randomness from a counter-based hash of (world seed, stage, turn, Dead index), never from one shared Rng stream consumed in horde order, or commit(speculate()) stops being bit-identical to step(). Keep the golden test in test_world.cpp passing."
        }
      ],
      "references": [
        "docs/design/scent-mobs.md"
      ],
      "depends_on": []
    },
