    {
      "id": "PEO-030",
      "order": 270,
      "type": "feature",
      "title": "Two-layer staggered scent field: near layer each turn, far layer by IIR",
      "status": "Pending",
      "severity": "S2",
      "effort": "L",
      "owner": "architect",
      "created": "2026-09-29",
      "notes": [
        {
          "at": "2026-09-29",
          "by": "architect",
          "text": "D-010 (2026-09-29): the far layer becomes a buildup layer. A cell's fade rate falls as the sliding 3x3 box total around it rises, to a nonzero minimum; box totals refresh on a turn schedule (every turn near the player, staggered further out); buildup pulls harder than a fresh trail. The separable IIR solve assumes a single decay everywhere, so re-examine the method (e.g. a coarse FTCS far layer stepped on a stagger) when briefing. Acceptance adds: a den where the player lingered, and a path walked often, both outlast and outpull a fresh trail."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-09-29",
          "by": "architect",
          "text": "PEO-007 constraint: compute D-010 fade rates (box totals) at the start of a turn from committed state, before the player's deposit is patched in, so speculate() sees the same rates commit() uses; the golden test must stay bit-exact. If a rate had to depend on this turn's deposit, commit would need to recompute every cell whose box includes the patched cells."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-09-29",
          "by": "architect",
          "text": "D-013 (2026-09-29) supersedes D-010's fade rule: buildup moves to a per-tile soak value (PEO-038), so the far layer returns to a single decay and D-008's separable IIR solve stands. Drop the buildup acceptance from this item; the doorway scenario stays."
        }
      ],
      "references": [],
      "depends_on": []
    },
